  "description": "Captures a world governed by a story nobody believes anymore. Adam Curtis's essay film: after the 1970s, politicians, financiers and then tech platforms built a simplified, manageable fake version of reality — and eventually everyone, including its builders, lost the ability to act outside it. Syria, Putin, Trump, Brexit and the algorithm feed as symptoms of one condition: hypernormalisation, where the fake is known to be fake and continues anyway.\n\nAdam Curtis explains how, at a time of confusing and inexplicable world events, politicians and the people they represent have retreated in to a damaging over-simplified version of what is happening.",
